NOTE: The AGPLv3 license of the thatteOS kernel does *not* cover user
programs that use kernel services through normal system calls, message-
passing IPC, or the thatteOS ABI — this is considered normal use of the
kernel, and does NOT make such programs "derivative works" or "works based
on" the kernel.

User-space programs written to run on thatteOS (or on the T3ISA emulator
hosting thatteOS) may therefore be distributed under any license of your
choice.

This note applies only to the system-call/ABI boundary. Code that is
statically linked INTO the kernel, kernel modules, or modified versions of
the kernel itself remain governed by the AGPLv3 in full.

(This follows the same principle as the syscall note in the Linux kernel's
COPYING file.)
